From 80c8c204d7f1af63f5059e9b055b4ad9d7219d50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:08:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mouse: battle views (map, cockpit, unit camera, rear):
 buttons, drags, wheel, edge scroll, battle pause menu

The game side (ga2_battlepointer.cpp) publishes the running view and the game's pad map
through ps2_mouse::setBattleState; the mouse then presses the game's own buttons:
map left/right/middle, Ctrl+click for order all, double click to focus, right drag to pan,
wheel to zoom, edge scrolling; cockpit left held = fire, right held = charge; unit camera
drag/wheel; middle held on the map = L2 (the angel list), wheel steps its cursor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
